@eurekaka 
The incorrect result is caused by the incorrect `PartitionColPos` [field](https://github.com/pingcap/tidb/blob/master/planner/core/point_get_plan.go#L259) in the `BatchPointGetPlan`. It's used to get the physical table id for each index [value](https://github.com/pingcap/tidb/blob/master/executor/batch_point_get.go#L212) and the following encoding will use it.
To fix this maybe we could add the set [logic](https://github.com/pingcap/tidb/blob/master/planner/core/point_get_plan.go#L662) for this field in `convertToBatchPointGet`.
These two statements could display the difference
```
// this will use the tryFastPlan path, the result is expected.
select * from t where (a, b) in ((1, 1), (2, 1));
// this will use the convertToBatchPointGet path.
select * from t where a in (2,1) and b = 1;
```
